/-- A member of the class, as the `3` orbit values it takes together with the proof that they name
one. `Magma.tupOK` is three tests: every orbit value is one the group's action allows, the operation
the tuple builds really is invariant, and no excess permutation is an automorphism of it. -/
@[reducible] def tup16R313 : Type := {w : Fin 3 → Fin 16 // Magma.tupOK S16R313.E S16R313.tr S16R313.z S16R313.st S16R313.X w = true}

/-- The class, as a family of magmas indexed by its own membership test. -/
@[implicit_reducible]
def srch16R313 (v : tup16R313) : Magma (Fin 16) :=
  Magma.mk (Magma.transport S16R313.E S16R313.tr v.1)

end Magma

/-! ### The source exhibits

`4` members of the class, chosen by greedy cover so that between them they model all `102` equations
that have a model in the class at all. Each check is `Magma.tupOK`: the tuple names a member of the
class. It is `native_decide` rather than `decide` because the invariance test is `256` cells times
the `320` group elements, which the elaborator will not walk inside its heartbeat limit.
-/

